  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (177 tests, 0 failed). Of those, 12 are new tests for the reservation behavior.\n\n**Store (`src/store.js`)**\n- `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release` follow your spec. Time comes only from the store's `clock`.\n- `removeItem` now checks against available stock rather than physical stock, so it can't remove reserved units.\n- Reservations are kept in memory after they expire. This lets `confirm` return `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` for them instead of `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`. They stop counting against availability as soon as they expire.\n- `confirm(id)` returns the reservation's sku, which the API uses for its response. You didn't ask for that.\n\n**API (`src/api.js`)**\n- `GET /stock/:sku` now also returns `available`.\n- `POST /reservations` returns 201 `{id}`, 409 `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` or 400 `INVALID_QTY`.\n- `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` returns 200 `{sku, stock}`, 404 `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND` or 410 `RESERVATION_EXPIRED`.\n- `DELETE /reservations/:id` returns 204 with a `null` body, including for ids that are unknown or already released.\n\n**Tests**\n- The new tests in `test/store.test.js` and `test/api.test.js` cover:\n  - reserve and its error cases;\n  - expiry at exactly creation time plus ttl;\n  - confirm, including after release or expiry;\n  - idempotent release;\n  - `removeItem` respecting reservations;\n  - the API status codes.\n\n`ttlMs` isn't validated, since the spec doesn't ask for it. A missing or non-numeric `ttlMs` makes the expiry `NaN`, so that reservation never expires.",
